---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Spidergraph — Personal Security Program"
  description="A free, open-source privacy and security program — a tiered playbook, seven interactive audit tools, and a live coverage radar chart. No backend, no accounts, no tracking."
  path=""
  current="home"
>
  <link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href={`${base}pages/home.css`} />

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">Spidergraph · Personal security program</div>
      <h1>
        See your whole <span>security posture.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Spidergraph is a complete privacy and security stack — from the tiered
        playbook that explains every control, to the interactive tools that
        audit what you actually have against it, plotted as one shape across
        every domain that matters.
      </p>
      <div class="flow">
        <span class="node">Read the Playbook</span>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <span class="node">Audit tools &amp; habits</span>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <span class="node">See your Spidergraph</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mystatus" id="myStatus">
      <div class="mystatus-head">
        <h3>Your Spidergraph</h3>
        <span class="hint">
          — read live from this browser's storage, nothing is fetched or sent
          anywhere
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="mystatus-grid" id="myStatusGrid"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="backup">
      <div class="backup-card">
        <div class="backup-head">
          <h3>Back up your data</h3>
          <span class="hint">
            — everything above lives only in this browser; save a copy before
            switching browsers, devices, or clearing site data
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="backup-actions">
          <button type="button" id="backupExportBtn" class="backup-btn primary">
            Download backup (.json) →
          </button>
          <button type="button" id="backupImportBtn" class="backup-btn">
            Restore from backup file →
          </button>
          <input
            type="file"
            id="backupFileInput"
            accept="application/json,.json"
            hidden
          />
        </div>
        <div class="backup-status" id="backupStatus"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid">
      <a class="card doc" href={`${base}playbook/`}>
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-code">DOC-01</span>
          <span class="card-type">Reference</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Personal Security Playbook</h2>
        <p>
          Twelve control domains, each tiered Budget → Mid → No-Limit, plus ten
          incident-response runbooks written in the Detect → Contain → Eradicate
          → Recover structure security teams actually use.
        </p>
        <div class="go">Read the playbook →</div>
      </a>

      <a class="card tool" href={`${base}privacy-stack-builder/`}>
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-code">TOOL-01</span>
          <span class="card-type">Interactive</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Privacy Stack Builder</h2>
        <p>
          Pick a target tier, select what you currently run across 15 product
          slots, and see live gap analysis, cost totals, and a radar chart of
          your coverage — modeled on a PC-part-picker build sheet.
        </p>
        <div class="go">Open the builder →</div>
      </a>

      <a class="card tool2" href={`${base}opsec-field-manual/`}>
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-code">TOOL-02</span>
          <span class="card-type">Interactive</span>
        </div>
        <h2>OPSEC Field Manual</h2>
        <p>
          44 behavioral controls across six domains — social engineering,
          physical security, legal documentation, operational discipline,
          incident readiness, and audit cadence. Habits, not purchases.
        </p>
        <div class="go">Start the audit →</div>
      </a>

      <a class="card tool3" href={`${base}broker-removal-tracker/`}>
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-code">TOOL-03</span>
          <span class="card-type">Interactive</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Broker Removal Tracker</h2>
        <p>
          Direct links to the official opt-out page for the ~16 highest-traffic
          people-search sites — Spokeo, BeenVerified, Whitepages, MyLife, and
          more — with your progress tracked locally as you work through them.
        </p>
        <div class="go">Start tracking →</div>
      </a>

      <a class="card tool4" href={`${base}breach-check-tracker/`}>
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-code">TOOL-04</span>
          <span class="card-type">Interactive</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Breach Check Tracker</h2>
        <p>
          List your own email addresses and aliases, then work through your own
          quarterly Have I Been Pwned check for each — this page tracks your
          progress locally, it never looks anything up for you.
        </p>
        <div class="go">Start tracking →</div>
      </a>

      <a class="card tool5" href={`${base}digital-legacy-worksheet/`}>
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-code">TOOL-05</span>
          <span class="card-type">Interactive</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Digital Legacy Worksheet</h2>
        <p>
          Organize who should be able to reach your accounts in an emergency and
          where recovery info lives — without ever writing down a live password.
          Export a working note, not a legal document.
        </p>
        <div class="go">Start the worksheet →</div>
      </a>

      <a class="card tool6" href={`${base}incident-response-card/`}>
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-code">TOOL-06</span>
          <span class="card-type">Interactive</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Incident Response Card</h2>
        <p>
          Fill in your own bank, card, and carrier fraud lines once, then print
          or export a compact card with the first three things to do — ready
          before you need it under pressure.
        </p>
        <div class="go">Build your card →</div>
      </a>

      <a class="card tool7" href={`${base}stuck-account-ledger/`}>
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-code">TOOL-07</span>
          <span class="card-type">Interactive</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Stuck Account Ledger</h2>
        <p>
          For accounts a service won't delete: generate plausible replacement
          details in your browser and record what you changed, where and when,
          so a reset question can't lock you out later.
        </p>
        <div class="go">Start the ledger →</div>
      </a>

      <a class="card gen" href={`${base}report/`}>
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-code">DOC-02</span>
          <span class="card-type">Generated</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Recommendations Report</h2>
        <p>
          Top picks per category, best practices to close any gap to 100%, and
          full source documentation — both the research trail behind this
          project and where to keep learning going forward.
        </p>
        <div class="go">View the report →</div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="about">
      <h3>How the pieces connect</h3>
      <p>
        The Playbook is the source of truth for every recommendation. The Stack
        Builder and OPSEC Field Manual audit your actual setup against it and
        can export a personalized version of the Recommendations Report
        reflecting your real selections — use the "Generate report" button
        inside either one rather than reading the static version here if you
        want your own results. The Broker Removal Tracker, Breach Check Tracker,
        Digital Legacy Worksheet, and Incident Response Card are narrower by
        design: flat checklists and worksheets that track your own progress and
        export their own plain-text (or printable) output, rather than scoring
        you against the Playbook's domains. Nothing you enter in any tool leaves
        your browser; there's no backend, no account, and no tracking — which
        also means this browser's storage is the <i>only</i> copy of your data.
        Use "Back up your data" above before clearing site data or switching
        browsers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script src={`${base}shared/persist.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}shared/backup.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}pages/home.js`} is:inline></script>
</BaseLayout>
